   </row>
   <row>
    <gid><![CDATA[58551]]></gid>
    <sid><![CDATA[687253]]></sid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Affinity for Technology Interaction]]></group_name>
    <group_order><![CDATA[2]]></group_order>
    <description><![CDATA[<p>The following questionnaire will ask you about your interaction with technical systems. The term “technical systems” refers to apps and other software applications, as well as entire digital devices (e.g., mobile phones, computers, TV, car navigation).</p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance/>
   </row>
   <row>
    <gid><![CDATA[58551]]></gid>
    <sid><![CDATA[687253]]></sid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Afinidade para a Interação Tecnológica]]></group_name>
    <group_order><![CDATA[2]]></group_order>
    <description><![CDATA[<p>De seguida, iremos fazer-lhe perguntas sobre a sua interação com sistemas tecnológicos. O termo "sistema tecnológico" refere-se a apps e a outras aplicações informáticas, bem como a dispositivos digitais [e.g., telemóvel, computador, televisão, sistemas de navegação automóvel (GPS)].</p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[pt]]></language>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance/>
   </row>
   <row>
    <gid><![CDATA[58565]]></gid>
    <sid><![CDATA[687253]]></sid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Augmented Reality Interfaces]]></group_name>
    <group_order><![CDATA[3]]></group_order>
    <description><![CDATA[<h4 style="text-align: center;">Read Carefully</h4>

<p data-end="642" data-start="335">Communicating with <strong>Autonomous Vehicles (AVs)</strong> is not always straightforward. While with traditional vehicles we can look at the driver and understand their intentions through<strong> gestures</strong> or <strong>eye contact</strong>, the absence of a driver in AVs can create <strong>uncertainty</strong> for pedestrians. In this study, we use <strong data-end="713" data-start="671">V2X technology</strong>, which allows vehicles to communicate with other road users and road infrastructure to help understand their intentions.</p>

<p data-end="642" data-start="335"><strong data-end="376" data-start="335">Imagine you are wearing an AR headset</strong> that connects to traffic and provides <strong data-end="437" data-start="415">real-time messages</strong> in your field of view. You are now at a pedestrian crossing, and an AV is approaching.</p>

<p data-end="642" data-start="335">The following designs illustrate different ways AR can <strong data-end="639" data-start="580">inform you about the vehicle’s behaviour and intentions</strong>. Please rate each design based on how <strong data-end="2054" data-start="2045">clear</strong> it is to you.</p>

<p><img src="/upload/surveys/687253/images/AR.png" style="width: 800px; max-width: 90%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; display: block;" /></p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance/>
   </row>
   <row>
    <gid><![CDATA[58565]]></gid>
    <sid><![CDATA[687253]]></sid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Interfaces de Realidade Aumentada]]></group_name>
    <group_order><![CDATA[3]]></group_order>
    <description><![CDATA[<h4 style="text-align: center;">Leia Atentamente</h4>

<p data-end="642" data-start="335">Comunicar com <strong>Veículos Autónomos (VAs)</strong> nem sempre é simples. Enquanto nos veículos tradicionais conseguimos olhar para o condutor e compreender as suas intenções através de <strong>gestos</strong> ou <strong>contacto visual</strong>, a ausência de um condutor nos VAs pode criar uma sensação de <strong>incerteza</strong> para os peões. Neste estudo, utilizamos a <strong data-end="713" data-start="671">tecnologia V2X</strong>, que permite que os veículos comuniquem com outros utilizadores da estrada e com a infraestrutura rodoviária para ajudar a compreender as suas intenções.</p>

<p data-end="642" data-start="335"><strong data-end="376" data-start="335">Imagine que está a usar uns óculos de RA</strong> que se ligam ao tráfego e fornecem <strong data-end="437" data-start="415">mensagens em tempo real</strong> no seu campo de visão. Neste momento, encontra-se numa passagem para peões e um VA está a aproximar-se.</p>

<p data-end="642" data-start="335">As ilustrações seguintes apresentam diferentes formas de RA para <strong data-end="639" data-start="580">informá-lo sobre o comportamento e intenções do veículo</strong>. Por favor, avalie cada design com base na sua <strong data-end="2054" data-start="2045">clareza</strong> para si.</p>

<p><img src="/upload/surveys/687253/images/AR.png" style="width: 800px; max-width: 90%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; display: block;" /></p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[pt]]></language>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance/>
   </row>
   <row>
    <gid><![CDATA[58579]]></gid>
    <sid><![CDATA[687253]]></sid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Interações por Voz]]></group_name>
    <group_order><![CDATA[4]]></group_order>
    <description><![CDATA[<h4 style="text-align: center;">Leia Atentamente</h4>

<p>Além dos ecrãs de RA, os <strong data-end="2596" data-start="2578">comandos de voz</strong> também podem ajudá-lo a comunicar com os VAs. Imagine que está numa passagem para peões e pode <strong data-end="2706" data-start="2678">falar diretamente com o VA</strong> para lhe dar instruções, como parar, abrandar ou avançar. Vamos explorar quão <strong data-end="2782" data-start="2772">adequados</strong> podem ser diferentes comandos de voz.</p>

<p><img src="/upload/surveys/687253/images/Speaking.png" style="width: 800px; max-width: 90%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; display: block;" /></p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[pt]]></language>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance/>
   </row>
   <row>
    <gid><![CDATA[58579]]></gid>
    <sid><![CDATA[687253]]></sid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Voice Interactions]]></group_name>
    <group_order><![CDATA[4]]></group_order>
    <description><![CDATA[<h4 style="text-align: center;">Read Carefully</h4>

<p>In addition to AR displays, <strong data-end="2596" data-start="2578">voice commands</strong> could also help you communicate with AVs. Imagine you are at a crosswalk and can <strong data-end="2706" data-start="2678">speak directly to the AV</strong> to instruct it to stop, slow down, or proceed. Let's explore how <strong data-end="2782" data-start="2772">applicable</strong> different voice commands might be.</p>

<p><img src="/upload/surveys/687253/images/Speaking.png" style="width: 800px; max-width: 90%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; display: block;" /></p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance/>
   </row>
   <row>
    <gid><![CDATA[58587]]></gid>
    <sid><![CDATA[687253]]></sid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Interações por Gestos]]></group_name>
    <group_order><![CDATA[5]]></group_order>
    <description><![CDATA[<h4 style="text-align: center;">Leia Atentamente</h4>

<p>Imagine um VA a aproximar-se enquanto espera numa passagem para peões. Em vez de falar, <strong data-end="3399" data-start="3374">utiliza gestos manuais</strong> para comunicar com o veículo. Quão <strong data-end="3450" data-start="3437">intuitivos</strong> lhe parecem os seguintes gestos?</p>

<p><img src="/upload/surveys/687253/images/Gesturing.png" style="width: 800px; max-width: 90%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; display: block;" /></p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[pt]]></language>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance/>
   </row>
   <row>
    <gid><![CDATA[58587]]></gid>
    <sid><![CDATA[687253]]></sid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Gesture Interactions]]></group_name>
    <group_order><![CDATA[5]]></group_order>
    <description><![CDATA[<h4 style="text-align: center;">Read Carefully</h4>

<p>Imagine an AV approaching as you stand at a crosswalk. Instead of speaking, <strong data-end="3399" data-start="3374">you use hand gestures</strong> to communicate with the vehicle. How <strong data-end="3450" data-start="3437">intuitive</strong> do you find each of the following gestures?</p>

<p><img src="/upload/surveys/687253/images/Gesturing.png" style="width: 800px; max-width: 90%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; display: block;" /></p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance/>
   </row>
   <row>
    <gid><![CDATA[58609]]></gid>
    <sid><![CDATA[687253]]></sid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Associar comandos de voz a gestos]]></group_name>
    <group_order><![CDATA[6]]></group_order>
    <description><![CDATA[<h4 style="text-align: center;">Leia Atentamente</h4>

<p data-end="818" data-start="670">Em algumas situações, os comandos de voz podem não ser suficientes—<strong data-end="765" data-start="729">acompanhá-los com um gesto</strong> pode tornar a comunicação mais clara e intuitiva.</p>

<p data-end="1204" data-start="1102">Para cada comando, <strong data-end="1175" data-start="1120">selecione o gesto que usaria mais provavelmente</strong> para reforçar a sua mensagem.</p>

<p><img src="/upload/surveys/687253/images/Gesturing_and_Speaking.png" style="width: 800px; max-width: 90%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; display: block;" /></p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[pt]]></language>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance/>
   </row>
   <row>
    <gid><![CDATA[58609]]></gid>
    <sid><![CDATA[687253]]></sid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Combining Voice Commands with Gestures]]></group_name>
    <group_order><![CDATA[6]]></group_order>
    <description><![CDATA[<h4 style="text-align: center;">Read Carefully</h4>

<p data-end="818" data-start="670">In some situations, voice commands alone may not be enough—<strong data-end="765" data-start="729">accompanying them with a gesture</strong> can make communication clearer and more intuitive.</p>

<p data-end="1204" data-start="1102">For each command, <strong data-end="1175" data-start="1120">please select the gesture you would most likely use</strong> to reinforce your message.</p>

<p><img src="/upload/surveys/687253/images/Gesturing_and_Speaking.png" style="width: 800px; max-width: 90%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; display: block;" /></p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance/>
   </row>
  </rows>
 </groups>
